Let me also double-check the neighbor calculation one more time:

For cell (r, c) in a hex grid where each row is shifted right by 1:
- (r, c-1) - left
- (r, c+1) - right
- (r-1, c) - up-left (row above is shifted left by 1, so column c in row above is at actual column c+r-1, which is 1 less
than c+r)
- (r-1, c+1) - up-right (row above is shifted left by 1, so column c+1 in row above is at actual column c+1+r-1 = c+r, 
which is same as c+r)
- (r+1, c-1) - down-left (row below is shifted right by 1, so column c-1 in row below is at actual column c-1+r+1 = c+r, 
which is same as c+r)
- (r+1, c) - down-right (row below is shifted right by 1, so column c in row below is at actual column c+r+1, which is 1 
more than c+r)

This gives 6 neighbors, which is correct for a hex grid.

