return value.
- shift: remove head node, update head to next node, decrement count, return value.
- unshift: create new node, if empty, set head and tail, else set new node->next = head, head->prev = new node, head = 
new node, increment count.
- count: return count.
- erase: traverse list to find first node with value, remove it (adjust pointers), decrement count, return true; if not 
found, return false.

